heading: Do you want to proceed?
options: No | Yes
source: captured 2026-11-21 for 2.1.4: Claude Code 2.1.329 (the version on minipc2, installed from npm) run in a throwaway container on minipc under tmux at 134x48, against a local mock of the Messages API; tmux capture-pane. Every row is as Claude drew it (real); the text is the mock's (neutral, made up for the capture). No live pane was read. Auto mode, two background helpers started: the session could not reach auto mode's server-side check, so Claude asked for approval of an Agent call in place of it, with its options unnumbered, No first and highlighted, and "Esc to cancel · Tab to amend" under them. Nothing is drawn under the dialog.
